    {
      "additions": 8,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/hiyouga/LlamaFactory/blob/b3df129593e7d0766bc34ad925138533058bbd47/README.md",
      "changes": 8,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/hiyouga/LlamaFactory/contents/README.md?ref=b3df129593e7d0766bc34ad925138533058bbd47",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "README.md",
      "patch": "@@ -674,6 +674,14 @@ You can also use **[Easy Dataset](https://github.com/ConardLi/easy-dataset)**, *\n \n ### Quickstart\n \n+To try the CLI without training first, start an interactive chat with the provided Qwen3 configuration:\n+\n+```bash\n+llamafactory-cli chat examples/inference/qwen3.yaml\n+```\n+\n+The first run downloads the model configured in `examples/inference/qwen3.yaml`. Enter a prompt in the terminal to chat, and press `Ctrl+C` to exit.\n+\n Use the following 3 commands to run LoRA **fine-tuning**, **inference** and **merging** of the Qwen3-4B-Instruct model, respectively.\n \n ```bash",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/hiyouga/LlamaFactory/raw/b3df129593e7d0766bc34ad925138533058bbd47/README.md",
